details:
Edit `app/globals.css` to introduce CSS variables for destructive button background and foreground colors. Ensure variables are defined for both light and dark mode selectors (e.g., `--destructive`, `--destructive-foreground`). Choose red shades that meet WCAG AA contrast requirements. Example:

:root {
  --destructive: #ef4444;
  --destructive-foreground: #fff;
}
[data-theme='dark'] {
  --destructive: #b91c1c;
  --destructive-foreground: #fff;
}

Modify `tailwind.config.js` to extend the theme with the new destructive color variables. Use the `css` function or `theme` function to map Tailwind color keys to the CSS variables defined in `globals.css`. Example:

colors: {
  destructive: 'var(--destructive)',
  'destructive-foreground': 'var(--destructive-foreground)',
}

Restart the dev server if necessary to apply changes.
